Apply this domain algorithm to prepared evidence: Design monitoring that can distinguish progress, nonresponse, and unintended effects using supplied methods. Specify comparable locations, timing, and effort, and define what evidence would justify continuing, revising, or stopping an intervention.
For each field, return a value only when supported, source IDs, authority, one rejected alternative, and status established, disputed, unknown, or inapplicable. Preserve contrary evidence and distinguish observation from inference.
